4f:["$","$Lb5",null,{"children":[["$","$Lb6",null,{"title":"The config is rejected at startup with an unknown field","id":"the-config-is-rejected-at-startup-with-an-unknown-field","children":["$","p",null,{"children":["Almost every store spec is strict about unknown fields, so this is usually a\nfield placed at the wrong nesting level: ",["$","code",null,{"children":"eviction_policy"}]," on the wrapper\nrather than on the store, or a backend option one layer too high. Check what\nthe innermost brace you're inside actually is."]}]}],["$","$Lb6",null,{"title":"Every Action Cache lookup misses","id":"every-action-cache-lookup-misses","children":["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","code",null,{"children":"verify"}]," with ",["$","code",null,{"children":"verify_hash"}]," or ",["$","code",null,{"children":"verify_size"}]," true on an AC store. An AC entry's\nkey is the action digest and its value is a result message, so both checks\nfail by construction and every AC update is rejected, leaving nothing to hit.\nSet both false there, and use ",["$","code",null,{"children":"completeness_checking"}]," instead."]}]}],["$","$Lb6",null,{"title":"Cache hits point at blobs that no longer exist","id":"cache-hits-point-at-blobs-that-no-longer-exist","children":["$","p",null,{"children":["The Action Cache has no ",["$","code",null,{"children":"completeness_checking"}]," wrapper, so it hands out\nresults referencing outputs the CAS has since evicted. Add it with ",["$","code",null,{"children":"cas_store"}],"\npointing at the CAS store."]}]}],["$","$Lb6",null,{"title":"A ref_store name isn't found","id":"a-ref_store-name-isnt-found","children":["$","p",null,{"children":["The name is a store name from the ",["$","code",null,{"children":"stores"}]," array, matched exactly. Order does\nnot matter, so a forward reference is fine. A typo or a renamed store is the\nusual cause."]}]}],["$","$Lb6",null,{"title":"Everything got slower after adding dedup","id":"everything-got-slower-after-adding-dedup","children":["$","p",null,{"children":["Small blobs. A blob that fits in one chunk gains nothing and still costs an\nindex write plus an extra existence check on every read. Put a\n",["$","code",null,{"children":"size_partitioning"}]," above the dedup store and route small objects straight to\nthe backend."]}]}],["$","$Lb6",null,{"title":"Entries went missing after changing the shard list","id":"entries-went-missing-after-changing-the-shard-list","children":["$","p",null,{"children":"Placement is derived from the set of stores and weights. Changing it moves\nwhere blobs are looked for. Nothing rebalances, so treat it as a flush."}]}]]}]
